g\">confinement but if you feel as I do </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">you dont care for the imperfections </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">of my writings for my part a word of </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">consolation from any sourse is </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">cordially recieved by </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">us</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> me I feel like </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">Joseph in Egyept doth my friends </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">yet live</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7467525612657915733\"><a href=\"#7467525612657915733\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 43:7, 27; 45:3.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> if they live do they remem</span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ber me have they regard for me if so </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">let me know it in time of trouble</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7535638332286917962\"><a href=\"#7535638332286917962\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans19\"><span id=\"documenttrans19\">19</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalms 27:5; 37:39; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-july-1828-dc-3\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-july-1828-dc-3\" poptitle=\"Revelation, July 1828 [D&amp;C 3]\">Revelation, July 1828</a> [D&amp;C 3:8].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">my Dear </span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8557509766246242404\"><a href=\"#8557509766246242404\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per86\" person=\"per86\" title=\"Emma Hale Smith\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">Emma</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Smith, Emma Hale\"><p>10 July 1804–30 Apr. 1879. Scribe, editor, boardinghouse operator, clothier. Born at Willingborough Township (later in Harmony), Susquehanna Co., Pennsylvania. Daughter of Isaac Hale and Elizabeth Lewis. Member of Methodist church at Harmony (later in Oakland...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/emma-hale-smith\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> do you think that my </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">being cast into prison by the mob </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">of</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">renders me less worthy of your friends</span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ship no I do not think so but </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">when I was in prisen and ye viseted </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">me inasmuch as you have don it to </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the least </span>&lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">of</span>​&gt;<span class=\"josephswriting\"> these you have don it to </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">me these shall enter into life </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">Eternal</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15995369295497775837\"><a href=\"#15995369295497775837\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans20\"><span id=\"documenttrans20\">20</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 25:36, 40, 46. <a href=\"/person/emma-hale-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Emma Smith</a> visited JS three times in the Clay County <a href=\"/place/jail-liberty-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">jail</a>: on 8–9 and 20–22 December 1838 and on 21 January 1839. (<span class=\"title\">History of the Reorganized Church,</span> 2:309, 315.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">The History of the Reorganized Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.</span> 8 vols. Independence, MO: Herald Publishing House, 1896–1976. </p></div></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> but no more</span></div><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><div class=\"right wasptag\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">your Husband J Smith Jr </span> [p. [3]]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/431/431_ms155_2_03_003_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/431/431_ms155_2_03_003_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/431/431_ms155_2_03_003.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/431/431_ms155_2_03_003_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/431/431_ms155_2_03_003.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "431", "requestedPageNumber": "3", "numberOfPages": "4", "editorialTitle": "Letter to Emma Smith, 21 March 1839", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to Emma Smith, 21 March 1839", "date": "March 21, 1839", "handwriting": "Handwriting of JS", "footnotes": [{"id": "9469740242242552761", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Extant copies of the 20 March 1839 <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839\" poptitle=\"Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839\">epistle</a> are in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/edward-partridge\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Edward Partridge</a> and <a href=\"/person/albert-perry-rockwood\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Albert Perry Rockwood</a>. (JS, Liberty, MO, to the Church and Edward Partridge, Quincy, IL, 20–25 Mar. 1839, copy, CHL; JS et al., Liberty, MO, to the Church and Edward Partridge, Quincy, IL, 20 Mar. 1839, copy, Albert Perry Rockwood, Mormon Letters and Sermons, 1838–1839, Western Americana Collection, Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library, Yale University, New Haven, CT.)</p></body></html>", "number": 14, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": "<p id=\"source-note1\">Smith, Joseph. Letter, Liberty, MO, to the Church and Edward Partridge, Quincy, IL, 20–25 Mar. 1839. Copy. CHL.</p><p id=\"source-note2\">Western Americana Collection. Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library, Yale University, New Haven, CT.</p>"}, {"id": "15162371468536651362", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">JS was perhaps referring to the history that he began in April 1838. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-march-september-1838/20\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-march-september-1838\" poptitle=\"27 April 1838 • Friday\">JS, Journal, 27</a> and <a href=\"/paper-summary/journal-march-september-1838/23\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers-text/tooltip/journal-march-september-1838\" poptitle=\"30 April 1838 • Monday\">30 Apr. 1838</a>; Historical Introduction to <a href=\"/intro/introduction-to-history-drafts-1838-1842\" class=\"article\">History Drafts, 1838–ca. 1841</a>.)</p></body></html>", "number": 15, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": "<p id=\"source-note1\">Western Americana Collection. Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library, Yale University, New Haven, CT.</p>"}, {"id": "10735312567292119174", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">Page torn</span>]r fo[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">page torn</span>]”.</p></body></html>", "number": 16, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "10701081345623752427", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">The prisoners apparently had some money in the <a href=\"/place/jail-liberty-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">jail</a>, presumably provided by individuals in <a href=\"/place/far-west-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Far West</a>. While imprisoned, <a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a> sent twenty dollars to his wife, <a href=\"/person/mary-fielding-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Mary Fielding Smith</a>, in <a href=\"/place/quincy-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Quincy</a>. (Hyrum Smith, Liberty, MO, to Mary Fielding Smith, Quincy, IL, 23 Mar. 1839, Mary Fielding Smith, Collection, CHL; see also Kimball, “History,” 100–101.)</p></body></html>", "number": 17, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": "<p id=\"source-note1\">Smith, Mary Fielding. Collection, ca. 1832–1848. CHL. <a href=\"https://catalog.churchofjesuschrist.org/record/a5a4b8a7-777a-4d83-90d3-f3c9646eeb96?view=browse\" class=\"externalLink\">MS 2779</a>.</p><p id=\"source-note2\"> Kimball, Heber C. “History of Heber Chase Kimball by His Own Dictation,” ca. 1842–1856. Heber C. Kimball, Papers, 1837–1866. CHL. MS 627, box 2.</p>"}, {"id": "7467525612657915733", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 43:7, 27; 45:3.</p></body></html>", "number": 18, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "7535638332286917962", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalms 27:5; 37:39; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-july-1828-dc-3\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-july-1828-dc-3\" poptitle=\"Revelation, July 1828 [D&amp;C 3]\">Revelation, July 1828</a> [D&amp;C 3:8].</p></body></html>", "number": 19, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "15995369295497775837", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 25:36, 40, 46. <a href=\"/person/emma-hale-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Emma Smith</a> visited JS three times in the Clay County <a href=\"/place/jail-liberty-missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">jail</a>: on 8–9 and 20–22 December 1838 and on 21 January 1839. (<span class=\"title\">History of the Reorganized Church,</span> 2:309, 315.)</p></body></html>", "number": 20, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": "<p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">The History of the Reorganized Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.</span> 8 vols. Independence, MO: Herald Publishing House, 1896–1976. </p>"}], "meta": {"/paper-summary-PageTitle": "Letter to Emma Smith, 21 March 1839, Page 3", "/paper-summary-MetaTitle": "Letter to Emma Smith, 21 March 1839, Page 3", "/paper-summary-MetaDescription": "I want you to have the Epistole coppyed immedeately